/* MTI6-GTADWIY-COCKPIT — STAR avatar + expressions
 * (owner-designated 2026-11-16; Embodiment Build 1, 2026-11-16)
 *
 * Daniel (owner) designated his own uploaded portrait as STAR's
 * face on 2026-11-16. The transparent cutouts were produced
 * locally (background removed on this machine from his uploaded
 * photo and from expression edits of it; the photo and the
 * full-size cutouts live outside the repo in the owner's files),
 * resized to 512x512 and encoded as WebP data URIs because this
 * repo ships text assets only — the app fetches NOTHING at
 * runtime.
 *
 * STAR_AVATAR_SRC is the idle face. STAR_AVATAR_EXPRESSIONS holds
 * the expression faces: talking (mouth open mid-speech), thinking
 * (gaze up-and-to-the-side), smile (warm closed-mouth smile).
 * Which expression SHOWS is decided by STAR's real UI state in
 * js/modules/star.js and js/shell-chrome.js — never by a timer:
 * the panel's reply-production state drives "talking", the
 * reply-completion transition drives "smile", and "thinking" is
 * shipped but deliberately unbound (the chat flow has no separate
 * pre-reply state to hang it on; see js/modules/star.js).
 *
 * Regenerate with tests/build-star-avatar.js (Pillow via the
 * local rembg venv). Consumers: js/shell-chrome.js (the STAR
 * launcher) and js/modules/star.js (the STAR panel figure +
 * header). Both treat this file as OPTIONAL: if STAR_AVATAR_SRC
 * is missing or an image fails to load, STAR keeps its original
 * glyphs (launcher ✨, header 🌟) exactly as before, and any
 * missing expression falls back to the idle face.
 */
window.STAR_AVATAR_SRC = "data:image/webp;base64,";
window.STAR_AVATAR_EXPRESSIONS = {
  talking: "data:image/webp;base64,",
  thinking: "data:image/webp;base64,",
  smile: "data:image/webp;base64,"
};
